cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper."
title: "Pricing Defects in Evaluation Environments by Expected Loss: A Probe Battery, the Floor It Had to Beat, and Twelve of Its Own Claims That Broke"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Theodoro
    given-names: Caio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7343-981X"
date-released: 2026-11-23
repository-code: "https://github.com/caiotheodoro/assay"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - RL environments
  - benchmark auditing
  - expected loss
  - reward hacking
  - pre-registration
  - negative results
abstract: >-
  A probe battery that prices defects in RL environments and eval suites by expected
  loss, compared against the trivial arm that flags everything, with the splits where
  the saving does not separate and the published claims the repository broke in itself.
  The code is Apache-2.0, the paper CC BY 4.0.
